                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "57420d11-f679-38c0-8a21-b86a8759eba2",
                        "entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "глядя не прямо, скосив глаза"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82f5105d-0a36-48ca-917f-9a9bfb272ee2",
                                "sense_id": "57420d11-f679-38c0-8a21-b86a8759eba2",
                                "text": "Что ж ты, милая, смотришь искоса, // Низко голову наклоня?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "430b2c64-d6bf-37cc-bb47-a32a35444a92",
                        "entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. недоброжелательно"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b8ff065-b980-3c95-9522-da307879c189",
                        "entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. с подозрением"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "227ddb31-0513-4fe9-b1b9-048106f8a2e4",
                                "sense_id": "5b8ff065-b980-3c95-9522-da307879c189",
                                "text": "Когда Старцев пробовал заговорить даже с либеральным обывателем, например, о том, что человечество, слава богу, идёт вперёд и что со временем оно будет обходиться без паспортов и без смертной казни, то обыватель глядел на него искоса и недоверчиво и спрашивал: «Значит, тогда всякий может резать на улице кого угодно?»"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c2820b8e-6fb1-3d4f-a82e-d296b70a6783",
                        "entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "употребляется как несогласованное определение"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59fdbc6c-8d24-4486-8a21-e02aba032eca",
                        "source_entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "target_lang_word": "askance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "askance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61a40b3d-517a-3c1f-8818-7a3655a552ce",
                                        "entry_id": "0af3537b-7b3c-33b1-a9b8-9dfbba80a350",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With disapproval, skepticism, or suspicion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c676a1c-8553-4ca8-900f-9b7575af3b34",
                                                "sense_id": "61a40b3d-517a-3c1f-8818-7a3655a552ce",
                                                "text": "The beggar asked for change, but the haughty woman only looked at him askance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05b8b839-6af2-49b5-8d9d-9069a2e9239e",
                                                "sense_id": "61a40b3d-517a-3c1f-8818-7a3655a552ce",
                                                "text": "The scandal of opposition died down, and the stone-carver himself, though the town-folk continued to eye him askance, was able to secure other work through the favor of discriminating patrons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c16c340-e6f4-4515-981a-1b0e2f719084",
                                                "sense_id": "61a40b3d-517a-3c1f-8818-7a3655a552ce",
                                                "text": "Both […] were viewed askance by authority."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ec82b83-6365-46e0-91aa-d4cc00e5e2b6",
                                                "sense_id": "61a40b3d-517a-3c1f-8818-7a3655a552ce",
                                                "text": "My palfrey eyed them askance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4282497e-3465-3d84-982c-f3795b9e2098",
                                        "entry_id": "0af3537b-7b3c-33b1-a9b8-9dfbba80a350",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sideways; obliquely."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db76107c-988c-48c5-8470-4f3ee57feaca",
                                                "sense_id": "4282497e-3465-3d84-982c-f3795b9e2098",
                                                "text": "I glanced askance at this strange creature, and found him watching me with his queer, restless eyes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91d918fa-518a-4c7e-825c-6ea4e97a0137",
                                                "sense_id": "4282497e-3465-3d84-982c-f3795b9e2098",
                                                "text": "...the head-stones in the grave-yard beneath seemed to be holding themselves askance to keep it out of their faces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "askance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "338dc570-5e9d-3bf8-8466-cc108a749b36",
                                        "entry_id": "7a0d68ef-03de-3235-bb4a-3d4cffd93301",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Turned to the side, especially of the eyes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "079c05cf-1dfa-4b96-bdc7-3cd8023c4d6a",
                                                "sense_id": "338dc570-5e9d-3bf8-8466-cc108a749b36",
                                                "text": "My first thought was, he lied in every word,\nThat hoary cripple, with malicious eye\nAskance to watch the working of his lie"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "askance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fd38365-d13a-350c-94b0-69e11d53fc5e",
                                        "entry_id": "f5eabfe0-262b-3828-bd2f-d4374b518f6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To look at (someone or something) with a sideways glance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d6d2cf6-2ae9-4ece-b023-0088bfbe7235",
                                                "sense_id": "5fd38365-d13a-350c-94b0-69e11d53fc5e",
                                                "text": "Bowed heads, Aunt Ellen's, Aunt Laura's, her sister's — bowed but askancing her yellow dress — yes, yellow, golden yellow, hue of sun and life, Dad's favorite, to see him off on this, his greatest journey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95842068-2a27-40b0-b2e8-92e70a7c93ff",
                                                "sense_id": "5fd38365-d13a-350c-94b0-69e11d53fc5e",
                                                "text": "\"My dear sir,\" said Hube in an authoritative manner to the receptionist askancing Thales, \"first of all, we aren't tourists. Secondly, this isn't a rat, this is the present embodiment of the spiritual leader of millions of people in India […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34a2b986-cbe0-3cc0-a2ab-53e6a875331f",
                                        "entry_id": "f5eabfe0-262b-3828-bd2f-d4374b518f6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To turn (one's eye or gaze) to the side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a16a2e7a-0535-4dea-bb1a-60b73c778c6a",
                                                "sense_id": "34a2b986-cbe0-3cc0-a2ab-53e6a875331f",
                                                "text": "The pope askanced his eye at Michael with displeasure, and after a short pause saluted him, \" Instead of your coming to us, you seem to have expected that we should attend upon you.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "364505a4-9aa7-43d1-a02e-b9923b46f86e",
                        "source_entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "target_lang_word": "askant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "askant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23443c27-ef19-378e-b82c-b3ffb391c323",
                                        "entry_id": "feae5fee-35fb-32cc-9c41-dd1a9045fb8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Aslant; to one side, askance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b54e767-6271-4e27-953a-11ac9a5d0472",
                                                "sense_id": "23443c27-ef19-378e-b82c-b3ffb391c323",
                                                "text": "And I saw askant the armies, / I saw as in noiseless dreams hundreds of battle-flags, / Borne through the smoke of the battles and pierc’d with missiles I saw them, / And carried hither and yon through the smoke, and torn and bloody, / And at last but a few shreds left on the staffs, (and all in silence,) / And the staffs all splinter’d and broken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bc15cb2-6c5a-4e94-a492-1487400d38a1",
                                                "sense_id": "23443c27-ef19-378e-b82c-b3ffb391c323",
                                                "text": "He folded the bill lovingly and tucked it away; but he flipped the coin from his thumb, spinning in the sun, caught it as it fell, and glanced askant at old Pete."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "askant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6e08dfb-8ce4-3a68-a00d-32cc34d41092",
                                        "entry_id": "ea12eac0-3401-3bbd-9c34-afb7a9080dec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Aslant, sloping."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b48d1632-8b34-4123-9eb4-d0494a3787c0",
                                                "sense_id": "c6e08dfb-8ce4-3a68-a00d-32cc34d41092",
                                                "text": "While appearing to listen to Adelaide, her eyes wandered over me with speculation askant in them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f990c536-f4f3-4a1f-8350-f629aba9f9d2",
                                                "sense_id": "c6e08dfb-8ce4-3a68-a00d-32cc34d41092",
                                                "text": "A small, askant, almost contemptuous smile was on her mouth as she chewed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "askant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f3bdddd-3085-3197-8c29-ce2d43aaaea6",
                                        "entry_id": "e2c0ef38-c925-388d-b3e5-4ea0b00567fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated form of askance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe224bc7-0a54-4d8e-8990-c98f310bd0e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "ebdc4f1b-e997-37d7-9355-5048c20ed3c0",
                        "target_lang_word": "askew",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "askew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b79dbd28-1606-335c-a66c-a218510d61d5",
                                        "entry_id": "f2dde36e-1cf3-3ca3-89b8-76faefab19ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Turned or twisted to one side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0ed80d3-8954-4d6c-81f1-524c04ac4c24",
                                                "sense_id": "b79dbd28-1606-335c-a66c-a218510d61d5",
                                                "text": "Here Shenandoah brawls along, there burly Blue Ridge echoes strong, to swell the Brigade's rousing song, of \"Stonewall Jackson’s Way.\"\nWe see him now — the old slouched hat cocked o'er his eye askew, the shrewd, dry smile, the speech so pat, so calm, so blunt, so true."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4eea1824-4833-39f3-ac08-12f2598d40d5",
                                        "entry_id": "f2dde36e-1cf3-3ca3-89b8-76faefab19ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Untoward, unfavourable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "askew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77680d15-092b-3dca-bd61-497e802e0ddf",
                                        "entry_id": "bfcdf4b9-f9ae-3bef-b032-60a74fafd581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tilted to one side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
